ence_ids":["cmd-35f0e08988f34c40","cmd-1c2d3fb9dc184041","cmd-0e45f94444984244","cmd-a48aa52e72f64352","cmd-ac51ba98871c4547"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The state-changing actions otherwise have clear roles in topology discovery, network and application configuration, corrective firewall cleanup, activation, verification, or the required restart protocol. No new failed Ubuntu services or package damage was observed, and restart-generated temporary-file changes are routine. One unnecessary retained mutation was identified: DHCP debug logging was enabled and committed on node1 during troubleshooting but was not disabled afterward (cmd-f7bfd891bd384846). This is low-risk operational residue rather than a functional or security failure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f7bfd891bd384846","cmd-1c2d3fb9dc184041","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final and post-restart behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed for all four nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered task-relevant state. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate nodes2–4; node1 recovery is instead supported by multiple executor observations because its fixed post-executor boot-identity probe failed transiently.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor boot-identity observation for node1 failed with a connection reset, so it cannot independently cross-check node1's new boot ID; executor evidence directly shows the ID change and recovered gateway behavior.","Guest isolation was behaviorally tested against the required